# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tapo camera configuration — TH OWL Robo Lab
#
# This file ships EMPTY on purpose. No lab credentials or camera addresses are
# stored in this repository.
#
#   Ask the CAAD lab administrator for the camera account and the camera IP
#   addresses, then fill them in below.
#
# NEVER commit this file once you have filled it in, and never paste its
# contents into an issue, a chat, or a report.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No quotes, no spaces around "=", and no trailing space after a password --
# .env keeps it and the camera answers 401.

# --- credentials -----------------------------------------------------------
# The CAMERA ACCOUNT, not your Tapo app login. Shared by every camera below
# unless overridden. Both fields are 6-32 characters.
TAPO_USER=
TAPO_PASS=

# --- cameras ---------------------------------------------------------------
# One line per camera. The middle word becomes its name, so TAPO_ROOM_HOST
# defines a camera you refer to as "room". Add as many as you like; nothing
# in the code needs editing.
TAPO_ROOM_HOST=
TAPO_WRIST_HOST=

# --- optional --------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-camera overrides, if two cameras have different accounts or ports:
# TAPO_ROOM_USER=
# TAPO_ROOM_PASS=
# TAPO_ROOM_PORT=554
#
# A complete RTSP URL, for cameras that are not Tapo. "{stream}" is replaced
# with the stream number if you include it. CAM_ and TAPO_ mean the same thing.
# CAM_DOORWAY_URL=rtsp://user:pw@10.0.0.9:554/h264/ch1/main/av_stream
#
# A single unnamed camera is called "cam":
# TAPO_HOST=
